  "decisions": [
    "Enabled is necessary preference but never local activation or authority. Metadata never installs executable transport.",
    "Configuration/provider replacement revokes all activations and attempts; newer explicit refresh supersedes only the same source, without remote timestamp merging.",
    "Random runtime ID plus monotonic local generations and request/source/provider correlation prevent stale/ABA/cross-runtime confusion.",
    "Only endpoint/format/conditional validators and correlation metadata reach source transport; labels, collections, disclosure preferences, identity and vault fingerprints are absent.",
    "304 requires the exact originally issued hint/provider/source/endpoint and base body digest, an empty body and null content type.",
    "Actual existing cached bytes are bounded/hashed under the live final runtime guard before the final host CAS callback. The host must atomically verify persisted source/generation/body presence/digest in that same durable transaction.",
    "Omitted304 validators retain issued values; validators observed from a different redirect endpoint are not promoted into reusable original-source cache validators.",
    "Cancellation cannot retract a synchronous final transaction already accepted; cancel returns false at/after that boundary. Later recheck errors do not roll back an already validly committed transaction.",
    "Final cache callback cannot reenter the session: try-lock fails closed instead of deadlocking.",
    "No HTTP/XML/durable cache backend implementation is supplied or qualified. Native/TS adapters currently compose one explicitly installed source provider; portable Rust supports multiple descriptors."
  ],
  "storage_limit": "Async staging is supported. The final durable CAS must complete synchronously under the live runtime guard. IndexedDB or other asynchronous final-store transactions require a separately qualified shared persistent-generation/CAS design and are not supported by this v1 boundary. Pre/post await checks alone do not close that race.",
  "limitations": [
    "Deterministic host fixtures exercise real async bindings and CAS protocol, not public DNS/TLS/HTTP/XML or a durable storage backend.",
    "Web-target WASM is instantiated in Node; this is not browser UI acceptance.",
    "Swift uses newly generated matching host bindings during the check; the mutable task-cache artifacts are not packaged release artifacts.",
    "No Apple app/device/signing/install, custody, issued provider-v1, main Command or issued ontology changes.",
    "Async final stores such as IndexedDB require a separately qualified shared persistent-generation transaction.",
    "Source imports remain inactive; metadata never installs executable transport or grants network authority."
  ],
